            Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey is the better protein powder for most people, because it gives 24 g of protein in about 120 calories, while Muscle Milk Genuine needs about 270 calories to deliver 32 g. Muscle Milk wins on two things: price, where Pro Series costs about $1.25 per 25 g of protein against Gold Standard's $1.49 at the Amazon prices we saw, and calories, if you are trying to gain weight. Both brands have powders listed in the NSF Certified for Sport directory.
